! 3C-SiC: the piezoelectric tensor on an **ultrasoft** dataset.
!
! Nothing in the assembly of `e_(k)ij = dP_k/d(eps_ij)` is norm-conserving, and
! the displacement leg of the same mixed derivative is the Born charge, which is
! validated on all three pseudopotential kinds. What was missing was a *crystal*:
! every ultrasoft and PAW case committed here is centrosymmetric, and an
! odd-rank tensor vanishes identically in one -- so all three routes agree on
! zero however wrong the strain leg is.
!
! Zincblende SiC is the cell that answers it. `-43m`, so nothing forces the
! tensor to zero and `e_14 = e_25 = e_36` is the only surviving component; two
! ultrasoft datasets, so `becsum` and the augmentation charge both carry the
! strain. Both pseudopotentials were already committed for other cases.
!
! `nosym`/`noinv` on an unshifted grid, for `alas-raman.in`'s two reasons: the
! crystal class must be what the answer comes out as rather than something an
! average imposed, and a shifted Monkhorst-Pack grid is not closed under the
! point group. `ecutwfc`/`ecutrho` are `sic-berry.in`'s.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    prefix = 'sic'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 8.24, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 24.0, ecutrho = 192.0,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si 28.086 Si.pz-n-rrkjus_psl.0.1.UPF
 C  12.011 C.pz-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 C  0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 0 0 0
